meta {
  name: List Tools
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/mcp
  body: json
  auth: basic
}

auth:basic {
  username: {{mcpUsername}}
  password: {{mcpPassword}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
}

body:json {
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 2,
    "method": "tools/list"
  }
}

docs {
  Lists the tools exposed to agents.

  Database access — `whoami`, `list_connections`, `list_schemas`, `list_tables`,
  `describe_table`, `run_query` — is read-only.

  `create_artifact` / `update_artifact` / `get_artifact` / `list_artifacts` /
  `archive_artifact` write D-Pilot's own document store, never a target database.

  `create_write_request` saves a **DRAFT** write request for a human to review; it
  executes nothing, on any environment. There is deliberately no tool to submit,
  approve or run one — that step happens in D-Pilot, as a person, so the paired
  verify SELECT gets read and (off direct-write envs) a second person approves.
}
